  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1220 PM MDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nThe 2nd jet maxima offshore of CA is forecast to close off a 2nd\nupper low over SoCal on Friday. Ample shear and sufficient\ninstability will persist Friday for another round of convection,\nwith a few strong to severe storms possible across much of central\nNM. The upper low is forecast to move east across southern AZ\ntoward NM on Saturday, brining a more widespread showers\nw/embedded storms scenario that will favor central/eastern NM\nthrough Saturday night. The upper low is then forecast to lift\nnortheast over the region Sunday, focusing precipitation chances\nacross the eastern plains and northern mountains. A Flash Flood\nWatch may be required for portions of eastern NM on Sat/Sun. Weak\nridging aloft will follow the departing upper low Monday through\nWednesday, bringing a slow warming/drying trend. Wet conditions\nmay return by the end of next week as an active troughing pattern\npersists with abundant Pacific moisture availability.",
